      "credit": "Ann Porteus from Tasmania, Australia",
      "license": "CC BY 2.0",
      "description": "Beautifully carved Mangbetu harp which I have been holding in my collection for the past 15 years. See images for detail and condition. Vermin damage to the skin and other marks are part of its African history. the white mark is paper that has been pasted to it when I purchased.\nThe stem is blackened wood and possibly ebony wood although I have not tested it.\nI do think it has some age.\nMeasures 65 x 40 x 20cm.\nAUD 2.500\nYou can see full size image. Click Action tab - Lower right 3 dots. Scroll, click on view all sizes.\nFurther information or more images of individual pieces please contact:\nAnn Porteus\nSidewalk Tribal Gallery\n19-21 Castray Esplanade,\nBattery Point 7004\nHobart Tasmania Australia\nann@sidewalkgallery.com.au\nsidewalktribal.com\nt: 613 6224 0331\n&lt;a href=\"https://www.flickr.com/photos/sidewalk_tribal_galleries/collections/\"&gt;www.flickr.com/photos/sidewalk_tribal_galleries/collections/&lt;/a&gt;\n\n&lt;a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/ann.porteus\" rel=\"nofollow\"&gt;www.facebook.com/ann.porteus&lt;/a&gt;",
